ral","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"October 30, 1985-January 5, 1986"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":5}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/cleveland-exhib-whistler-1988","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"The View from Afar: Whistler and the Japanese Print","seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/cleveland-exhib-whistler-1988","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"クリーブランド美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/クリーブランド美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"1988年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/1988"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"August 9-October 16, 1988"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":11}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2012-rinpa-aesthetic","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Designing Nature: The Rinpa Aesthetic in Japanese Art","description":[{"@value":"\"Rinpa\" is a modern term that refers to a distinctive style of Japanese pictorial and applied arts that arose in the early seventeenth century and has continued through modern times. Literally meaning \"school of Korin,\" Rinpa derives its name from Ogata Korin (1658–1716), a celebrated painter from Kyoto. It embraces art marked by a bold, graphic abbreviation of natural motifs, frequent reference to traditional court literature and poetry, the lavish use of expensive mineral and metallic pigments, incorporation of calligraphy into painting compositions, and innovative experimentation with new brush techniques."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://www.metmuseum.org/-/media/images/exhibitions/2012/rinpa-aesthetic/rinpa_poster2.jpg?w=600","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2012-rinpa-aesthetic","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2012/rinpa-aesthetic","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2012～2013年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2012-2013"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"May 26, 2012–January 13, 2013"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":116}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2013-birds-in-the-art-of-japan","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Birds in the Art of Japan","description":[{"@value":"This exhibition presents approximately 150 works in various media from medieval times to the present. Highlights include a unique, early seventeenth-century pair of ink-painted screens showing a flock of 120 mynah birds in flight or strutting on the shore; and a set of four enormous paintings of birds of prey by the nineteenth-century master Kawanabe Kyōsai, each over nine feet high. Displays of paintings will be juxtaposed with examples of modern and contemporary textiles, ceramics, lacquerware, and bamboo art. Drawn mostly from the Museum's own collection, it will also feature some fifteen works on loan from private collections."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/51ba32eae8eb54b2973e45b4a7865719a3f8c30b-481x334.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2013-birds-in-the-art-of-japan","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2013/birds-in-the-art-of-japan","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2013年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2013"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"February 2–July 28, 2013"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":142}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2013-brush-writing","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Brush Writing in the Arts of Japan","description":[{"@value":"In the East Asian tradition, handwriting was thought to reflect one's personality, but not in the sense of Western graphology, or handwriting analysis. Rather, through the copying of revered models and through creative innovation, a distinctive handwriting style conveyed one's literary education, cultural refinement, and carefully nurtured aesthetic sensibilities."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/88c8bc1ce12778497261ab4a5b9b8067ec76b393-481x720.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2013-brush-writing","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2013/brush-writing","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2013～2014年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2013-2014"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"August 17, 2013–January 12, 2014"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":185}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2014-edo-period-painting","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"The Flowering of Edo Period Painting: Japanese Masterworks from the Feinberg Collection","description":[{"@value":"Displaying exemplary works from painting schools that arose in Japan in the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, the exhibition allows viewers to discover how Japanese painting evolved from the traditional modes of Chinese and Japanese (Yamato-e) styles that had prevailed through medieval times.... Rather than focus on the orthodox output of the Tosa and Kano ateliers, which dominated artistic production in the late medieval period, The Flowering of Edo Period Painting highlights the new, exuberant styles of the Rinpa, Nanga, Maruyama-Shijō, and Ukiyo-e schools, as well as independent painters of the Edo period."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/2c211cfeed327c76cee41f13e2678d7f0244fc2c-481x615.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2014-edo-period-painting","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2014/edo-period-painting","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2014年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2014"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"February 1–September 7, 2014"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":66}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2014-kimono","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Kimono: A Modern History","description":[{"@value":"The Arts of Japan Galleries have been transformed into a dazzling fashion show of kimono from the late eighteenth century to the present day. Translated literally as \"thing to wear,\" the kimono has gone through major transformations throughout history: in the Edo period (1615–1868) it was an everyday garment, and now it is worn mainly on special occasions and collected as \"traditional Japanese art.\" ... Highlights also include three examples of contemporary kimono created by designers designated by the Japanese government as Living National Treasures."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/ee585aeb3cad9b196676a261bad92da3af07496a-481x248.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2014-kimono","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2014/kimono","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2014～2015年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2014-2015"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"September 27, 2014–January 19, 2015"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":161}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2015-celebrating-the-arts-of-japan","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Celebrating the Arts of Japan: The Mary Griggs Burke Collection","description":[{"@value":"This tribute to a great collector reveals the distinctive features of Japanese art as viewed through the lens of 50 years of collecting: the sublime spirituality of Buddhist and Shinto art; the boldness of Zen ink painting; the imaginary world conjured up by the Tale of Genji and classical Japanese literature; the sumptuous colors of bird-and-flower painting; the subtlety of poetry, calligraphy, and literati themes; the aestheticized accoutrements of the tea ceremony; and the charming portraiture of courtesans from the \"floating world\" (ukiyo-e)."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/1471299e4e8059e8f245897eb9cb1553c7fd86a5-1013x1080.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2015-celebrating-the-arts-of-japan","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2015/celebrating-the-arts-of-japan","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2015～2017年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2015-2017"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"October 20, 2015–May 14, 2017"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":162}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2015-discovering-japanese-art","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Discovering Japanese Art: American Collectors and the Met","description":[{"@value":"The 2015 centennial of the Department of Asian Art offers an ideal opportunity to explore the history of the Museum's collection of Japanese art. Showcasing more than two hundred masterworks of every medium, this exhibition tells the story of how the Museum built its comprehensive collection of Japanese art beginning in the early 1880s, when it owned just a small, eclectic array of Japanese decorative arts."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/a2c17bc2b111aa7da606fcca742ddf4fd87415fb-481x325.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2015-discovering-japanese-art","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2015/discovering-japanese-art","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2015年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2015"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"February 14–September 27, 2015"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":290}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2017-japanese-bamboo-art","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Japanese Bamboo Art: The Abbey Collection","description":[{"@value":"Featuring works of Japanese bamboo art dating from the late 19th century to the present—the period when basketry in Japan became recognized as an art form that transcends \"craft\"—this loan exhibition showcases more than 80 bamboo baskets and sculptures created by accomplished artists, including all six masters who have received the designation \"Living National Treasure.\" Highlighting key stages in the modern history of Japanese bamboo art, the exhibition is drawn from the Abbey Collection, one of the finest private collections of Japanese baskets and bamboo sculpture; most of the works have never before been presented in public."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/41e694135f670d52248f0e0f3e6e503aa48afeca-1013x1080.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2017-japanese-bamboo-art","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2017/japanese-bamboo-art","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2017～2018年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2017-2018"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"June 13, 2017–February 4, 2018"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":217}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2018-japanese-arms-and-armor","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Japanese Arms and Armor from the Collection of Etsuko and John Morris","description":[{"@value":"Presenting a wide array of samurai armor, blades, and accoutrements dating from the fifteenth to the nineteenth century, this exhibition celebrates the promised gift of thirty-seven objects from the collection of Etsuko and John Morris, as well as other important gifts made by Mr. and Mrs. Morris to The Met's Department of Arms and Armor over the past seventeen years."}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2018-japanese-arms-and-armor","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2018/japanese-arms-and-armor","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2018～2019年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2018-2019"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"January 25, 2018–January 6, 2019"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":0}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2018-poetry-of-nature","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"The Poetry of Nature: Edo Paintings from the Fishbein-Bender Collection","description":[{"@value":"Painting blossomed in Japan during the Edo period (1615–1868) as artists daringly experimented with conventional styles. In this exhibition, more than forty examples of Edo-period paintings from the collection of Estelle P. Bender and her late husband T. Richard Fishbein—mostly gifts and promised gifts to The Met—help trace the development of the major schools and movements of this fascinating era. Contemporary Japanese ceramics are juxtaposed with Edo-period paintings, while works in various formats and media from The Met collection provide context. The celebration of the natural world serves as a unifying theme, and the intertwined relationship between poetry and the pictorial arts—so fundamental to Japanese tradition—is a particular focus of the exhibition."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/10a96849dc53dc504016ca1054c399913911ae27-1013x1080.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2018-poetry-of-nature","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2018/poetry-of-nature","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2018～2019年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2018-2019"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"February 27, 2018–January 21, 2019"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":109}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2019-tale-of-genji","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"The Tale of Genji: A Japanese Classic Illuminated","description":[{"@value":"This is the first major loan exhibition in North America to focus on the artistic tradition inspired by Japan's most celebrated work of literature, The Tale of Genji...Highlights include two National Treasures and several works recognized as Important Cultural Properties. For the first time ever outside Japan, rare works are on view from Ishiyamadera Temple—where, according to legend, Shikibu started writing the tale."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://www.metmuseum.org/-/media/dd09b5b16c6547a9aa361fdd404cd3fc.ashx","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2019-tale-of-genji","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2019/tale-of-genji","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2019年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2019"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"March 5–June 16, 2019"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":135}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2021-japan-history-of-style","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Japan: A History of Style","description":[{"@value":"This exhibition celebrates how gifts and acquisitions of the last decade have transformed The Met’s ability to narrate the story of Japanese art by both expanding and deepening the range of remarkable artworks that can meaningfully elucidate the past. Each of the ten rooms that make up the Arts of Japan Galleries features a distinct genre, school, or style, representing an array of works in nearly every medium, from ancient times to the present. Highlights include the debut of a spectacular group of contemporary metalwork by Living National Treasures and emerging artists, and, in the first rotation, a selection of woodblock prints from the Lee E. Dirks Collection."}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/e4dbf2fe7cb2a411557ff76eefc4615a2c54120a-1080x1080.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2021-japan-history-of-style","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2021/japan-history-of-style","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"アメリカ","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/アメリカ"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"March 8, 2021–April 24, 2022"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":271}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/metmuseum-exhib-2023-anxiety-hope-in-japanese-art","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"Anxiety and Hope in Japanese Art","description":[{"@value":"Drawn largely from The Met’s renowned collection of Japanese art, this exhibition explores the twin themes of anxiety and hope, with a focus on the human stories in and around art and art making.\n\nThe exhibition begins with sacred images from early Japan that speak to concerns about death, dying, and the afterlife or that were created in response to other uncertainties, such as war and natural disaster. The presentation then proceeds chronologically, highlighting medieval Buddhist images of paradises and hells, Zen responses to life and death, depictions of war and pilgrimage, and the role of protective and hopeful images in everyday life. In the final galleries, the exhibition’s underlying themes are explored through a selection of modern woodblock prints, garments, and photographs. (from Metropolitan Museum of Art)"}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/cctd4ker/production/64d83ca072950196a80da3247ec89e5835418161-1920x983.jpg?w=640","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/metmuseum-exhib-2023-anxiety-hope-in-japanese-art","related":"https://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/anxiety-hope-in-japanese-art","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"メトロポリタン美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/メトロポリタン美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2023年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2023"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"2023-04-08/2024-07-14"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":106}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/mfa-exhib-2022-heros","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"THE HEROES　刀剣×浮世絵－武者たちの物語","description":[{"@value":"武者絵は『平家物語』のような軍記物語や武勇伝説に登場する英雄ヒーロー を描いた絵画です。浮世絵の祖と言われる菱川師宣の時代から、江戸後期の歌川国芳、明治期の月岡芳年にいたるまで、 多くの浮世絵師が武者絵を手掛けました。源頼光、源義経、上杉謙信、武田信玄などの武将のほか、スサノオノミコトの武勇、巴御前のような女武者の奮戦も描かれています。武者絵は伝統的に描き継がれたことで、時代を越えて広く親しまれていました。本展覧会では、世界最高水準の日本美術コレクションを誇るボストン美術館の所蔵品から厳選した刀剣と武者絵率100%の浮世絵版画、そして武者絵と共通のイメージがデザインされた刀剣の鐔つばを通じて、さまざまなヒーローたちの活躍をご紹介します。また、武者絵の世界をよりわかりやすくご紹介するため、国内コレクションからも刀剣、浮世絵を特別出品します。（公式サイトから）"}],"thumbnail":[{"@id":"https://macg.roppongihills.com/assets_c/2021/06/heroes_1280-thumb-450xauto-8383.jpg","@type":"dctypes:Image","format":"image/jpeg"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/mfa-exhib-2022-heros","related":"https://macg.roppongihills.com/jp/exhibitions/heroes/","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"森美術館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/森美術館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2022年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2022"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"2022-01-21/2022-03-25"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":90}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/minneapolis-exhib-2021-japan","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"ミネアポリス美術館　日本絵画の名品","description":[{"@value":"This exhibition showcases masterpieces from this collection of Japanese art, with a focus on Edo-period paintings, including works by artists from the Kano school and Rinpa tradition, as well as ukiyo-e artists. Through this selection of masterly works by widely admired artists, including Sesson Shūkei, Kano Sansetsu, Itō Jakuchū, Soga Shōhaku, Katsushika Hokusai, and Tōshūsai Sharaku, the exhibition traces the evolution of Japanese painting while also giving a sense of the intentions of the American collectors fascinated by Japanese art who acquired these works and later bequeathed or donated them to the museum.","@language":"en"},{"@value":"本展は、Miaの日本美術コレクションの中から、中世から近代にいたる日本絵画の変遷を選りすぐりの優品でご紹介します。水墨画・狩野派・やまと絵・琳派・浮世絵・文人画（南画）・奇想派・近代絵画というように、江戸絵画を中心に日本絵画史の主要ジャンルをほぼ網羅するラインナップで、初の里帰り作品を含む貴重な機会です。","@language":"ja"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/minneapolis-exhib-2021-japan","metadata":[{"property":"http://schema.org/spatial","label":"Spatial Label","value":"東京都","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/place/東京"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2021年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2021"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"April 14–June 27, 2021"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":111}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-emaki","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"絵巻物等","description":[{"@value":"国立公文書館デジタルアーカイブの「資料いろいろ―絵巻物等」から"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-emaki","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0200000000/0201050000/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":9}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-hakubutsu","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"博物図等","description":[{"@value":"国立公文書館デジタルアーカイブの「資料いろいろ―博物図等」から"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-hakubutsu","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0200000000/0201010000/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":10}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-icp-kobunsho","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"重要文化財（公文書）","description":[{"@value":"国立公文書館が所蔵する重要文化財のうち公文書に区分されるもの。"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-icp-kobunsho","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0600000000/0601000000/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":135}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-kuniezu","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"重要文化財（国絵図等）","description":[{"@value":"The Tokugawa Shogunate ordered four times in years of Keicho, Shoho, Genroku and Tempo to prepare maps of every \"kuni\" (country) all over Japan."},{"@value":"江戸幕府の命で、慶長・正保・元禄・天保の4回、全国規模で国ごとの絵図等が作成されました。"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-kuniezu","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0300000000/default/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":163}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-maps","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"地図・図面等","description":[{"@value":"国立公文書館が所蔵する地図・図面資料を紹介します"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-maps","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0200000000/0405000000/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":93}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-mikikigusa","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"視聴草","description":[{"@value":"Mikikigusa (total 176 volumes) containing information and records written or filed by direct retainer Miyazaki Narichika during closing days of Edo period abounds with many interesting illustrations and beautiful color diagrams. Some of them are shown here."},{"@value":"江戸末期の旗本宮崎成身が、さまざまな資料や情報を記録しあるいは綴じ込んだ『視聴草』（全176冊）には、興味深い図版や美しい彩色図が多数含まれています。"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-mikikigusa","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0200000000/0202000000/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":7}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/najda-vexhib-sensai","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"全国主要都市戦災概況図","description":[{"@value":"Drawings of Air-raid damaged sites of major cities in Japan was prepared in December, 1945, by Records Department of First Demobilization Ministry to notify outline of Air-raid damage to repatriates. The foreword of the document mentions the importance of this survey and necessity of making quick adjustment after finding that the first question asked by repatriating military personnel and civilian employees of the military landing on Japanese shores was generally about Air-raid damage."},{"@value":"昭和20（1945）年12月、戦災の概況を復員帰還者に知らせるために、第一復員省資料課によって、全国主要都市戦災概況図は作成されました。まえがきには、当時帰還しつつあった復員軍人軍属の内地上陸にあたっての質問第一声が、概ねまず戦災概況についてであることを知り、この調査の重要性とその迅速な調整の必要とを痛感した、と述べられています。"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/najda-vexhib-sensai","related":"https://www.digital.archives.go.jp/DAS/pickup/view/category/categoryArchives/0200000000/0203000000/00","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"国立公文書館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/国立公文書館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":132}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/parisjp-exhib-2018-jomon","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"縄文―日本における美の誕生--パリ日本文化会館","description":[{"@value":"「ジャポニスム2018」としてフランス・パリの日本文化会館おいて「縄文―日本における美の誕生」展を開催します。東京国立博物館で開催された特別展「縄文－一万年の美の鼓動」を再構成し，縄文時代の美を体現する国宝火焔型土器をはじめとした土器に加え，土偶や装身具など，国宝や重要文化財を含む縄文時代を代表する造形を展示します。（公式サイトから）"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/parisjp-exhib-2018-jomon","related":"https://www.bunka.go.jp/seisaku/kokusaibunka/bunkazaihogo/kobijutsu_kaigaiten/1410026.html","metadata":[{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#accessInfo","label":"Access","value":"パリ日本文化会館","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/chname/パリ日本文化会館"},{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2018年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2018"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"2018-10-17/2018-12-08"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":37}]},{"@id":"https://api.cultural.jp/iiif/2/exhibition/pushkin_tnm-exhib-2018-edo","@type":"sc:Collection","label":"江戸絵画名品展--プーシキン美術館","description":[{"@value":"平成30年度は「ロシアにおける日本年」であることを受け，文化庁と東京国立博物館は，所蔵の江戸絵画作品を中心として，千葉市美術館，板橋区立美術館などが所蔵する作品に，ロシア所在の優品を加えて展示する「江戸絵画名品展」を開催することとなりました。この展覧会では，武家好みの瀟洒な作風により幕府御用絵師として江戸絵画の基調を確立した狩野探幽をはじめとした狩野派諸家の作品はもとより，江戸時代中期の文化の多様化を反映した円山応挙，与謝蕪村，伊藤若冲，曽我蕭白など京都諸派による個性豊かな作品，日本美術が海外で注目される嚆矢となり，ジャポニスムの大きな影響を世界に生み出した浮世絵や琳派の作品，特に昨今世界的ブームとなっている葛飾北斎や尾形光琳などの作品を含んだ名品135件により，江戸時代絵画の魅力を紹介するものです。（公式サイトから）"}],"seeAlso":"https://ld.cultural.jp/data/pushkin_tnm-exhib-2018-edo","metadata":[{"property":"http://schema.org/temporal","label":"Temporal Label","value":"2018年","id":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/entity/time/2018"},{"property":"https://jpsearch.go.jp/term/property#temporal","label":"JPS Temporal","value":"2018-09-04/2018-10-28"},{"property":"http://schema.org/workFeatured","label":"Count of Work Featured","value":112}]}]}